    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0156" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg144"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/1997: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Oslo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-04-09T07:00:00+01:00">April 9, 1940—7
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Norwegian Government left for Hamar 3 hours inland from Oslo at 7 a.m. I am
                    proceeding there by motor with other heads of missions. All Foreign Service
                    Officers remaining in Oslo. At request of British and French Ministers this
                    Legation has taken over British and French interests. Oslo is quiet, as public
                    has not yet realized situation. Foreign Office states that Norwegian forces are
                    resisting the German advance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
